# Line endings are pinned to LF everywhere.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default) checks every text
# file out with CRLF while esbuild and Vite emit LF. The committed bundles in
# runtime/dist then differ from a fresh build on every line, which makes a
# build-drift guard in CI fail for a reason that has nothing to do with drift.
#
# No .bat or .cmd files are tracked here; those are the only ones that would
# genuinely need CRLF. PowerShell reads LF fine.
* text eol=lf


*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
